# Technical settings single-truth

Active technical values live in canonical Product System component settings.
Documentation explains them. Calculation code consumes them. Intake does not administer them.

For any adjustable technical or business parameter: one canonical active value, one owner, typed identity, visible source, projected to Product System UI.

Do not scatter the same active value through docs, Intake fields, or anonymous code literals.

Software implementation constants stay in code. Not every constant needs a setting.

When a canonical setting exists, retire old active sources. Do not keep compatibility copies.

Do not add fake admin Edit/Save until persistence, validation, versioning, and owner authorization exist.
